# Agent stack — historical May 2026 baseline (reviewed 27/10/2026)

> **Important:** Previous model defaults reflected a May 2026 snapshot and have been replaced by a runtime-verified routing rule, **not** a claim about the current Cursor picker. Use the current runtime model/entitlement and [27 October engineering model register](../../engineering-system/MODEL-ROUTING.md). The repository's fleet policy currently excludes Cursor as a reviewer; founder proposal to add Cursor requires an explicit policy change, not a silent bypass.

> Cursor official 2026 updates: [Changelog](https://cursor.com/changelog), [Agent SDK announcement (20 October)](https://prod.cursor.com/en-US/changelog).

## Model routing (runtime-verified; replaces historical May defaults)

| Context | Required behaviour |
|---------|--------------------|
| Interactive coding or review | Record installed/approved actual model; pick tier through the documented [routing policy](../../engineering-system/MODEL-ROUTING.md) and local task results |
| Background tasks | Run only authorised scoped agents with cost, file ownership, retry cap and JEV evidence |
| High-risk architecture | Strong builder plus independent Codex review under existing policy; no unapproved Cursor review lane |

Historical evidence only: https://cursor.com/changelog/composer-2-5

## Hooks (Indy Dev Dan contract)

- PreToolUse shell hook: `node .cursor/hooks/pre-bash-validate.cjs`
- Hook stdout must be **one JSON line only**: `{"permission":"allow"}` or `{"permission":"deny",...}`
- Never use bare `echo` in `.cmd` when stdin is piped
- Smoke test: `powershell -File scripts/test-cursor-prebash-hook.ps1`
- Troubleshooting: `.cursor/HOOKS-FIX.md`, skill `cursor-hooks-windows`

## Karpathy-inspired execution

1. State assumptions; ask if unclear — do not guess.
2. Simplest correct diff — no speculative features.
3. Surgical edits — only what the task requires.
4. Goal-driven verification — run commands, paste output before claiming done.

Banned: "should work", "probably passes", "seems correct".

## gstack (selective)

- Enabled globally: **`/qa`**, **`/cso`** only (explicit invocation).
- Do not auto-run other gstack commands — Synthex skill catalog covers CEO/design/ship.
- Do not run `./setup --team` in this repo.

## Codex CLI

- Keep `@openai/codex` updated (`npm i -g @openai/codex@latest`) for optional sidecar review.
- `codex-adversarial` is **manual only** on auth/payments/migrations — never in autonomous loops.

## CI merge policy

- **Blocking:** GitHub Actions (Build, tests, lint, security gates).
- **Ignorable unless branch protection requires it:** `Vercel – synthex-sandbox`.
- **Use for preview QA:** `Vercel – synthex` preview URL on the PR.

